\par \pard\plain \s54\loch\qj\widctlpar\sb30\sa60\fs22\fi0\li360\lin360\ltrpar{\loch
Get input and validate the data, putting valid data into provided string. }
\par \pard\plain \s54\loch\qj\widctlpar\sb30\sa60\fs22\fi0\li360\lin360\ltrpar{\loch
Prompt user to input a string of a max length: maxLength. Then take the stream into inputWordString from stdin, only taking in the }{\loch\b\loch
STRING_LENGTH_MAX}{\loch
 number of characters. Check both if the string is greater than 0 characters with a newline. Also that the string terminates with a newline before the end of the fgets() string so that we know it is within }{\loch\b\loch
STRING_LENGTH_MAX}{\loch
. If it is, break the loop as we have a valid string being pointed to. If not check if the string is too long or too short.'}
\par \pard\plain \s54\loch\qj\widctlpar\sb30\sa60\fs22\fi0\li360\lin360\ltrpar{\loch
'If it's not greater than 1 newline character, give error message for that.'}
\par \pard\plain \s54\loch\qj\widctlpar\sb30\sa60\fs22\fi0\li360\lin360\ltrpar{\loch
'If the string isn't too short, loop through stdin until either a '\\n' or EOF character. This will clear stdin and ready it for new input. Also give the message that the string is too long. After the errors are printed and the stream is clear, the loop runs again, prompting until it recieves valid input.}
